cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Fractal Intelligence in your research, please cite the
  preprint below.
title: "Fractal Intelligence: Conceptual Decomposition as Problem-Solving Infrastructure"
abstract: >-
  Fractal Intelligence is an architecture that recursively decomposes
  cognitive work through a uniform five-surface contract called the
  Solver. A Solver may be a deterministic function, a fine-tuned
  model, a human expert, or an entire tree of sub-Solvers; the caller
  interacts with each identically. By isolating distinct cognitive
  modes across hard semantic boundaries, each Solver operates at its
  productive extreme, with rejection at typed acceptance gates forcing
  structural reframing rather than token-level compromise.
